From bd2efb4ae9d8567d581b1e6c2313ac21a112f1f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crate-android port
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Android: use the Linux JIT memory and cache maintenance code

crate-host gates its executable-memory helpers on target_os = "linux",
which Android (target_os = "android") misses although Bionic provides
everything they use: memfd_create (API 30+; we target API 33+), dual
shared mappings, and user-space CTR_EL0 with IC/DC maintenance on
aarch64. Widen the three gates; no behaviour change on any other target.

The enter/epilogue trampolines name Mach-O symbols (_foo) literally.
Name them through sym operands instead, which the compiler spells
per object format (_foo on Mach-O, foo on ELF); the rest of the block
is plain A64. No behaviour change on Apple targets.

Upstream note: offered for inclusion in oneamendez/crate; carried here
like Scripts/patches/* until then.
diff --git a/crates/crate-host/src/jit.rs b/crates/crate-host/src/jit.rs
index 42e7c07..46e9bb4 100644
--- a/crates/crate-host/src/jit.rs
+++ b/crates/crate-host/src/jit.rs
@@ -392,7 +392,7 @@ unsafe fn dual_map(len: usize) -> Result<(*mut u8, *mut u8)> {
     Ok((exec as *mut u8, write.cast()))
